※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ Where the line is meant to stand as it is, the attribute says so.  It is
※ attached to the statement, which is the thing being spoken about.
※ 'ignore' and not 'expect': what is asserted here is that the line is allowed,
※ and 'expect' on an error says the construct is known to be wrong, which
※ discards the function it is in.
let count: u8 = 7u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    @[ignore(5005)]
    1u6
    @[ignore(5005)]
    count
    @[ignore(5005)]
    count & 3u8
    0u6
